---This is a copy of storage/googlesql/public/value.proto. ValueProto represents the serialized form of the googlesql::Value. The intention is to support multiple languages including Java and C++, so we must be sensitive to the distinction between Java Strings and byte arrays or ByteStrings. We also want to support use-cases which do not want to serialize a copy of the GoogleSQL type for every instance (which might be very repetitive). Therefore, unlike googlesql::Value, ValueProto does not carry full type information with every instance, and can only be fully interpreted with an associated TypeProto.
---@class gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.ValueProto
---@field jsonValue? string Tag 22 was used for json value as bytes, now obsolete. Json value represented as a string document.
---@field dateValue? number Primitive for date.
---@field uint32Value? number Primitive for uint32.
---@field int32Value? number Primitive value for int32.
---@field timestampPicoValue? string Encoded timestamp_pico value. For the encoding format see documentation for googlesql::TimestampPico::SerializeAsBytes().
---@field protoValue? string Stores a serialized protocol message.
---@field intervalValue? string Encoded interval value. For the encoding format see documentation for IntervalValue::SerializeAsBytes().
---@field uuidValue? string Encoded uuid value. For the encoding format see documentation for UuidValue::SerializeAsBytes().
---@field tokenlistValue? string Encoded tokenlist value. copybara:strip_begin(internal-comment) See //search/tokens:token_list. copybara:strip_end
---@field uint64Value? string Primitive for uint64.
---@field geographyValue? string Geography encoded using ::stlib::STGeographyEncoder
---@field boolValue? boolean Primitive for bool.
---@field int64Value? string Primitive for int64.
---@field mapValue? gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.Cloudbilling_Map Encoded map value. See go/googlesql_map.
---@field bignumericValue? string Encoded bignumeric value. For the encoding format see documentation for BigNumericValue::SerializeAsProtoBytes().
---@field ValueProtoSwitchMustHaveADefault? boolean User code that switches on this oneoff enum must have a default case so builds won't break when new fields are added.
---@field floatValue? number Primitive for float.
---@field bytesValue? string Primitive for bytes.
---@field enumValue? number Tag 11 was used for specifying micros timestamps as int64, now obsolete.
---@field numericValue? string Encoded numeric value. For the encoding format see documentation for NumericValue::SerializeAsProtoBytes().
---@field arrayValue? gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.Cloudbilling_Array An array of value
---@field structValue? gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.Struct A struct of values
---@field stringValue? string Primitive for string.
---@field timestampValue? string primitive for timestamp
---@field datetimeValue? gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.Datetime primitive for datetime
---@field doubleValue? number Primitive for double.
---@field timeValue? string Bit field encoding of hour/minute/second/nanos. See TimeValue class for details.
---@field rangeValue? gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.Range Encoded range value. See go/googlesql_range.

---@alias gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.ValueProtoList gcp.unstable.cloudbilling_v1beta.ValueProto[]

